---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
---

<section class="box skills">
	<div class="stack gap-2 lg:gap-4">
		<Icon icon="terminal-window" color="var(--accent-regular)" size="2.5rem" gradient />
		<h2>Frontend</h2>
		<p>
			I like interfaces that feel fast, obvious, and a little polished around the edges. React, TypeScript, state
			management, design systems, weird browser bugs - all fair game.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="stack gap-2 lg:gap-4">
		<Icon icon="trophy" color="var(--accent-regular)" size="2.5rem" gradient />
		<h2>Backend</h2>
		<p>
			I enjoy the less glamorous stuff too: clean APIs, reliable data flows, service boundaries, and code that keeps
			behaving after everyone has stopped looking at it.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="stack gap-2 lg:gap-4">
		<Icon icon="strategy" color="var(--accent-regular)" size="2.5rem" gradient />
		<h2>Full-Stack</h2>
		<p>
			Best when I can zoom out, connect the dots, and ship the whole thing - from database shape to UI details to the
			"wait, what happens if..." edge cases.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.box {
		border: 3px solid var(--gray-100);
		border-radius: 1.25rem;
		padding: 1.5rem;
		background:
			linear-gradient(135deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--gray-999) 86%, transparent), transparent), var(--gradient-subtle);
		box-shadow:
			12px 12px 0 var(--accent-regular),
			var(--shadow-sm);
	}

	.skills {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3rem;
	}

	.skills h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
	}

	.skills p {
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.box {
			border-radius: 1.5rem;
			padding: 2.5rem;
		}

		.skills {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
			gap: 5rem;
		}

		.skills h2 {
			font-size: var(--text-2xl);
		}
	}
</style>
